{"id":"w63530","name":"Chocolate Chip Rolls","author":"Wikibooks Cookbook contributors","source":{"name":"Wikibooks Cookbook","url":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Chocolate_Chip_Rolls"},"via":{"name":"Wikibooks","url":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Chocolate_Chip_Rolls"},"image":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Chocolate-Chip-Roll-Broken-2006Feb24.JPG?width=640","cuisine":"","country":"","region":"Global","course":"dessert","protein":"veggie","diet":2,"allergens":131,"minutes":30,"time":{"prep":15,"cook":15,"passive":0,"passiveWhy":[]},"timeEstimated":true,"servings":"","difficulty":"easy","ingredients":[{"item":"Whole-wheat flour","qty":"2 cups / 240 g"},{"item":"White unbleached flour","qty":"2 cups / 250 g"},{"item":"Salt","qty":"1 tsp / 6 g"},{"item":"Baking powder","qty":"3 tsp / 13.8 g"},{"item":"Milk or soy milk","qty":"1 ½ cup (360 ml) / 366 g"},{"item":"Vegetable oil","qty":"½ cup (120 ml) / 109 g"},{"item":"Chocolate chips (or small chocolate pieces)","qty":""}],"steps":["Preheat oven to 425°F (210°C)","Mix dry ingredients together.","Mix liquid ingredients into dry.","Turn dough out onto floured baking cloth and knead slightly.","Roll dough into log, then cut into 8–12 pieces","Press pieces flat, sprinkle with chocolate chips, and roll up to enclose the chocolate.","Place rolls on greased baking sheet, and bake 13–15 minutes.","Serve fresh."],"tags":[],"youtube":"","culture":{"text":"This is a recipe grown out of an experiment on a traditional biscuit recipe; they\u0027re not extremely sweet, but fall closer to dessert than just rolls or biscuits.","source":{"name":"Wikibooks Cookbook","url":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Chocolate_Chip_Rolls"}},"license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","lifestyle":3,"era":"modern"}